// Package messaging is the shared messaging surface: the transport interface
// every Go surface speaks, the typed outcome vocabulary, the message-id and
// generation primitives, and #356's tool contract.
//
// schemas/ in this repository is the single source of truth for the merged
// messaging tools. Generated Go artifacts are checked in and kept current by
// `go generate ./internal/messaging/...`:
//
//   - schemas/message_route.umpire.json — the route-precondition table for
//     avenor_message, generated by umpire-go-gen into message_route.gen.go as
//     MessageRouteFields/MessageRouteConditions/Check. The router reads the
//     generated reasons for the two permission rules and for an invalid
//     action; every other row's text is a template from the conformance
//     fixture. Each field has one slot per rule kind, so no two rules share a
//     slot: the action enum is the check rule on action; control_reply support
//     is the enabledWhen slot on target and the resume caller rule is its
//     fairWhen slot; the two never-user-visible state guards (tell/ask want a
//     live target, resume wants a resumable one) are the enabledWhen and
//     fairWhen slots on message.
//   - schemas/message_route.conformance.json — the per-action input contract
//     (permitted keys, required keys, declared types), the repair templates and
//     the language-neutral conformance cases. Loaded at run time by
//     ApplicabilityTable, PeersApplicabilityTable and the two loaders; its
//     templates and applicability tables are also compiled into schema.gen.go.
//   - schemas/message.input.json and schemas/peers.input.json — the JSON
//     Schemas the Go surfaces publish to their SDK and the conformance test
//     validates against, compiled into schema.gen.go as string constants.
//   - schemas/message.outcome.json — the action-by-outcome matrix and the one
//     producer of result text, compiled into schema.gen.go.
//
// Nothing in this package imports a surface package: the router lives in
// internal/messaging/router so it may import this package and askclient
// together.
package messaging

//go:generate go run github.com/umpire-tools/umpire-go-gen@v0.1.1 -i ../../schemas/message_route.umpire.json -output-file message_route.gen.go -pkg messaging
//go:generate go run ./cmd/genschema -message-input ../../schemas/message.input.json -peers-input ../../schemas/peers.input.json -conformance ../../schemas/message_route.conformance.json -outcome ../../schemas/message.outcome.json -out schema.gen.go
